  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Negation rules in infinitive clauses",
     "texto": [
      "1. **Placement of nicht**: «Nicht» is usually placed right before the final block **zu + Infinitiv** or before the adverb or adjective being negated: **Er versprach, nicht zu spät zu kommen** (he promised not to arrive too late); **Ich habe vor, die Einladung nicht anzunehmen** (I intend not to accept the invitation).",
      "2. **Negation with kein-**: If a noun with indefinite article or uncountable object of the infinitive is negated, the declension of **kein-** is used: **Es ist ratsam, keine voreiligen Zugeständnisse zu machen** (it's advisable not to make hasty concessions); **Du brauchst keine Angst zu haben** (you don't need to be afraid).",
      "3. **Negative purpose**: «um … nicht zu» expresses \"so as not to\": **Ich beeile mich, um nicht zu spät zu kommen** (I hurry so as not to arrive late)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Type of negation",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Element",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Example",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
     "filas": [
